William Brodersen User Stories:
1. As a user, I want to log in using my login name, so that I can access the app
- Valid login_name logs user in
- Session is created
- Redirects to user detail view
2. As a user, I want to see my comment immedialetly after posting
- UI updates without page reload
- Comment includes text, user, and timestamp
3. As a user, I want my uploaded photo to appear immediately, so that I know it worked
-Photo shows in user's photo list
-Includes correct metadata (data, user)
4. As a user, I want my password to be hidden while typing, so that my information is private
- Password fields use masked input
- No plain text visible
Warren Itenson's User Stories:
1. As a user, I want to upload a photo from my device, so that I can store it in my account
 - “Add Photo” button is visible only when logged in
 - Clicking button opens file picker UI
 - User can select a file and submit
 - Backend POST /photos/new saves file in images/ with unique name
 - Database stores file reference, creation date, and owner
2. As a user, I want my uploaded photo to appear immediately, so that I know it worked
 - UI updates without full page reload
 - Photo shows in user’s photo list
 - Displays correct image from saved reference
3. As a user, I want a simple upload interface, so that I can easily add photos
 - Uses Material-UI components (button, dialog, file input)
 - Submit button is disabled until a file is selected
 - Shows success or error message after upload
 - Only accepts valid image file types
